Package: qupflowR
Title: Connect R and 'Shiny' to 'QuPath' Through a Local Bridge
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller", email = "58561665+r-heller@users.noreply.github.com",
 role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Development version of an interface between R and the 'QuPath'
 0.7.0 platform for digital pathology image analysis. The planned design
 lets R talk to a local 'Java' bridge (a 'QuPath' extension and a headless
 worker) over an authenticated loopback protocol, adds a 'Shiny' app that
 is built on the same R functions, and packages analysis workflows so they
 can be shared and run again. This version contains only the package
 foundations: classified error conditions, a message catalogue, protocol
 JSON helpers and a JSON Schema subset validator with the protocol
 schemas, plus a hash-pinned external-method execution boundary.
 The bridge client, the app and the workflow engine are not
 implemented yet.
